        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Manihot grahamii is a shrub or treelet in the family Euphorbiaceae."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "This fast-growing species is closely related to Manihot esculenta, the edible tapioca. Growing up to {{convert|3|m|ft|abbr=off|frac=2}} tall, it bears striking palmate leaves, and pale green bell-shaped flowers in summer. It is native to South America, including southern Brazil, Uruguay, Paraguay and Argentina."
          }
        ]
